{
  "explanations": [
    {
      "id": "F-D1-1b5bca2812",
      "text": "Multiple critical ORU systems (ORU-CRIT-H01 through ORU-CRIT-H14) are making undocumented calls to the lrc-db-01 database, as observed by the interface engine over 14 days. This lack of documentation hides a dependency that could cause unexpected impacts on lab result processing if the database changes or fails. The proposed fix involves 51 patch operations to record these dependencies in the CMDB."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D10-37ef3aa2dd",
      "text": "The backup for h02-pacs-cache-db has not succeeded since 2026-10-04T13:52:00Z, indicating a backup failure. Without reliable backups, patient imaging data stored in this cache could be lost or corrupted in a system outage. No patch operations are currently indicated; further investigation of the backup configuration is needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D9-b519fcc3ae",
      "text": "The protection path for h42-pacs-cache-db shows a drift between the CMDB and the observed backup target arr-h42-01 at site H42. This mismatch means the documented disaster‑recovery plan may not reflect the actual backup location, risking incomplete recovery. No patch operations are currently indicated; a review of the protection configuration is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D5-31dd79b7d2",
      "text": "The owner of ris-db-01 is recorded as NW-Imaging-Systems in the CMDB, but the observed owner is NW-DBA, based on five evidence points. An incorrect owner can lead to confusion about responsibility for changes, potentially delaying critical updates or incident response. The proposed fix consists of one patch operation to correct the owner field in the CMDB."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D9-7aa2a50db0",
      "text": "The protection path for h38-pacs-cache-db indicates a drift where the documented backup target does not match the observed target arr-h38-01 at site H38. This discrepancy could cause the backup strategy to be ineffective during a recovery scenario. No patch operations are currently indicated; a review of the protection settings is needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D10-d6475e6ab6",
      "text": "The backup for h35-labmw-db has not succeeded since 2026-10-02T09:43:00Z, signaling a backup failure. Failure to back up this laboratory database could jeopardize test results and patient care if data is lost. No patch operations are currently indicated; further investigation of the backup process is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D9-feeef47d89",
      "text": "The protection path for h17-labmw-db shows a drift between the CMDB and the observed backup target arr-h17-01 at site H17. This means the recorded disaster‑recovery plan may not align with the actual backup location, risking restore failures. No patch operations are currently indicated; a review of the protection configuration is needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D5-fe326c7991",
      "text": "The owner of ie-db-01 is recorded as NW-DBA in the CMDB, but the observed owner is HYD-Integration-Support, supported by six evidence points. An inaccurate owner record can impede accountability and slow response to issues affecting integration services. The proposed fix involves one patch operation to update the owner field in the CMDB."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D5-ebbb728ff2",
      "text": "The owner of lrc-db-01 is listed as NW-Lab-Systems in the CMDB, while the observed owner is HYD-Integration-Support, based on eight evidence points. This mismatch can create confusion about who is responsible for database changes, potentially affecting lab result reliability. The proposed fix consists of one patch operation to correct the owner in the CMDB."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D11-5a3435ebca",
      "text": "Data replication between stor-usw-01 and stor-cin-01 is occurring via the pod-vol-dwh-db-01-export path, which may violate data‑residency requirements. Unauthorized cross‑site replication could expose patient data to jurisdictions with different compliance rules, increasing legal risk. No patch operations are currently indicated; a review of the replication configuration is needed."
    }
  ]
}

